othing's rushing you i think that's  a perfect place to do it  just to like you know be human  and be vulnerable so i think it's  fantastic to do that  yeah i also echo leo and i was just  points um one of my favorite things this  past quarter was taking the bike out  because schwab and jmac lets you rent  out bikes for free  and biking to the tennis courts and the  golf bridge just i would go to tennis  and call for the fight back  with friends um and so that was amazing  um and i don't know our free time we  don't really have a lot of free time  because our time is filled  up with talking to people doing things  just hanging out like you have time  blocks we're hanging out at manzanita  field which is a new field that we have  next to schwab and so  it's always a busy time but it's a great  time  um real quick lightning answer  plus one on rich for walks um one of my  best friends at the gsp  i literally went on to walk with every  single week for two years  and we still do a call every two weeks  um and so that just shows you like the  the level  the real the deep relationship level  that you can form with someone  and then um yeah and then and then you  can literally  the nice thing about the gsp is they  give you budget to do any event you want  and so i held a bunch of like filipino  food dinner  events um i held board great  board game and ice cream night and then  anyone could just sign up and that was a  great way to meet people  and also try the best ice cream in the  bay area  for free i mean i guess you paid for it  through your tuition but  technically but yeah you get it back in  a way  awesome thank you all so much for  sharing those really heartfelt stories  um i loved hearing them and i'm sure our  attendees did too  so thank you so much to all of our  panelists for spending this  hour with us thank you to our  participants for submitting your really  thoughtful questions  please let us know in the poll when  you're thinking of joining us and i'll  